Z||000001||Dan||06-09-2001||08:54 AM||||Bump<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||06-09-2001||09:54 AM||||Actually, I think you're in a bit of a pickle. The previous owner will probably have to obtain a duplicate title then transfer it to you. Check with your DMV.<P>I dunno about your state, but in Georgia there is a guy at the tag office that runs the VIN to verify title applications (free) when an owner tries to register (pay tax) without adequate proof of title. <P>In my case it was my Fiero and the dealer I bought from was supposed to have done the title transfer. The tag office ran the VIN and it came up with the previous owner not me = no tag for Thomas   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I called the dealer and he had "forgotten". I drove directly over and picked up the papers in person, got my $18 fee back from him, and returned to the tag office and did the title and tag mydamnself.<p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||06-10-2001||10:39 PM|||| Anyone out there that can run a VIN check?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tweek||06-11-2001||12:21 AM||||The PO of my 84 didn't have the title, but lucky me, In the state of Maine, only cars '85 and up need titles.||||reg||1
